words.txt.gz is a generated correction dictionary (word<TAB>weight, gzip). It is built by
tools/build-dictionary.py from these free-licensed sources:

- English word frequencies: hermitdave/FrequencyWords, content/2018/en/en_50k.txt
  The frequency-list CONTENT is licensed CC BY-SA 4.0 (the project's own code is MIT; the data,
  derived from the OpenSubtitles corpus via OPUS, is CC BY-SA 4.0 per its README). Attribution:
  Hermit Dave, hermitdave/FrequencyWords, derived from OpenSubtitles (opus.nlpl.eu).
  https://github.com/hermitdave/FrequencyWords
  Because this word list derives from CC BY-SA 4.0 data, the generated words.txt.gz data asset is
  distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/), separately
  from the application code's AGPL-3.0-or-later license.

- First names: dominictarr/random-name, first-names.txt (public domain)
  https://github.com/dominictarr/random-name

- Surnames: dominictarr/random-name, names.txt (public domain)
  https://github.com/dominictarr/random-name

Names that carry no corpus frequency are assigned a fixed baseline weight so they are plausible
correction candidates without outranking genuinely common words. To regenerate:

    python3 tools/build-dictionary.py
